Changelog: 09-10-2026 13:56:58

The app now has a window: BC-250 Persistent ACPI (bc250_acpi_gui, PyQt6) shows whether the override is
installed, the CPU's frequency steps and idle states, and with Status with sudo whether the kernel loaded the
tables this boot. Install and Uninstall run the override script through sudo (masked password prompt, never
stored). A warning that asks "Continue anyway?" (no BC-250 GPU found, a BIOS that looks modded) is shown in a
dialog, and the install runs again with --yes only after Yes.

The override scripts moved into bc250-acpi-override.sh (--install, --uninstall, --status, --yes); the install
and uninstall steps are the same as in the old install.sh and uninstall.sh. Without a terminal, a warning stops
the install with exit code 3 instead of waiting for an answer. uninstall.sh is gone.

install.sh now installs the app like the other suite apps, as your own user: a root-owned copy in
/opt/bc250-persistent-acpi-v<version>, a venv with PyQt6, the launcher bc250-persistent-acpi-gui, an app menu
entry and a Desktop icon (--no-desktop-shortcut, --uninstall, --uninstall --purge). Installing the app changes
nothing on the board. Run as root, it stops and points at sudo ./bc250-acpi-override.sh --install.

New app icon, tests for the override script against a fake board and for the window, and README updated.

